# Stinging nettles: upright stalks with pairs of pointed, dark-green leaves, in dense patches on damp, rich ground - the
# edge of a wood, near the trunks, along the water. Head Leafy: Petals = leaves (in pairs up the stalk, two slots each),
# HeadSize = the bottom leaf's length, Open = how far they rise from flat; Color2 = the drooping flower catkins on top.
